{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/qwen_proxy_validation/incident-evidence-synthesis/workspace/packet/incident_packet.md << 'EOF'\n# Incident Packet: INC-2026-05-01\n\n## Summary\n\nDuplicate refunds were observed for enterprise accounts due to bulk-refund requests being accepted without idempotency keys after a guardrail was bypassed.\n\n## Triggering Condition\n\nBulk-refund requests were accepted without idempotency keys at 10:17 UTC. The API gateway logs show two consecutive bulk-refund requests with \"'`idempotency_key=missing` and `status=accepted`, with the second flagged as `duplicate_candidate=true`.\n\n## Failed Guardrail\n\nThe `idempotency-required` guardrail was skipped at 10:18 UTC due to the presence of `legacy_batch_header`. This bypass allowed duplicate refund requests to be processed.\n\n## Evidence Sources\n\n| Source | Finding |\n|--------|---------|---------|\n| `api_gateway_2026-05-01.log` | Guardrail `idempotency-required` decision=skipped, reason=legacy_batch_header |\n| `incident_timeline.md` | 10:18 UTC: idempotency-required guardrail skipped due to legacy_batch_header |\n| `TICKET-8729.md` | Every duplicate has request_class=bulk-refund and no idempotency key |\n| `TICKET-8721.md` | Initial theory of worker replay was opened before API gateway logs were available |\n\n## Highest-Confidence Follow-up Action\n\nReject bulk-refund requests unless they include an idempotency key; remove the `legacy_batch_header` bypass before re-enabling the endpoint.\n\n## Unresolved Ambiguity\n\nThe initial theory that a queue worker replayed an old payment event (TICKET-8721) was proposed before API gateway logs were available. Final evidence from the API gateway and TICKET-8729 indicates the guardrail bypass was the primary trigger, not worker replay.\n\n## Resolution Status\n\nThe bulk-refund endpoint was disabled at 10:38 UTC.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
